  "novel": "A [[corporate|corporate]] law firm [[offered|offer]] Ted a job with a huge salary. The money was [[tempting|tempting]], but Ted wanted to be an [[architect|architect]], not a [[lawyer|lawyer]]. He [[doubted|doubt]] himself.\n\nMeanwhile, a [[porn star|porn star]] named Ted Mosby [[surfaced|surface]] online. The [[revelation|revelation]] was [[hilarious|hilarious]] but [[damaging|damaging]] to Ted's [[reputation|reputation]]. Barney [[found|find]] it [[amusing|amusing]]. Ted did not.\n\nLily [[confessed|confess]] she had once [[manipulated|manipulate]] Ted's relationships. She had [[secretly|secretly]] [[sabotaged|sabotage]] dates she disliked. Ted was [[furious|furious]]. \"You had no right,\" he [[declared|declare]].\n\nIn the end, Ted rejected the corporate job. \"I'm not that guy,\" he said. He chose his passion over money. Some choices, he realized, defined who you were.",
